BT /F1 12 Tf 14 TL 72 720 Td (Salt and other minerals do not evaporate with the water. When seawater) Tj T* (evaporates, the salt is left behind. This is why rain is fresh water even though) Tj T* (much of it began in the salty ocean.) Tj T* () Tj T* (TRANSPIRATION) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (Plants also send water into the air. A plant takes up water through its roots) Tj T* (and carries it up through its stem to its leaves. The plant keeps only a small) Tj T* (part of this water. Most of it leaves through tiny openings in the leaves and) Tj T* (joins the air as water vapor. This is called transpiration.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Transpiration helps the plant in two ways. It pulls more water and nutrients up) Tj T* (from the soil, and it cools the leaves, much as sweating cools a person. A large) Tj T* (tree can give off hundreds of liters of water on a warm day, and a whole forest) Tj T* (puts a great deal of moisture into the air. This is one reason forests are often) Tj T* (damp and cool, and why cutting down large areas of forest can change the local) Tj T* (weather.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Scientists often put evaporation and transpiration together and call the) Tj T* (combined total evapotranspiration, because from far above it is hard to tell) Tj T* (which one a drop of vapor came from.) Tj T* () Tj T* (CONDENSATION) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (Water vapor rises into the sky, where the air is cold. As the vapor cools, its) Tj T* (particles slow down and cling together. The vapor turns back into tiny drops of) Tj T* (liquid water. This change from gas to liquid is called condensation.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The drops are so small and light that they float. Billions of them gather around) Tj T* (specks of dust and salt in the air, and together they form a cloud. A cloud is) Tj T* (not water vapor. It is a mass of tiny liquid drops, or in very cold air, tiny) Tj T* (ice crystals.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Condensation also happens close to the ground. The drops that form on the) Tj T* (outside of a cold glass on a warm day are water vapor from the room air) Tj T* (condensing on the cold surface. Morning dew on grass and the fog over a lake at) Tj T* (dawn form in the same way, when the air near the surface cools enough that its) Tj T* (vapor turns to liquid.) Tj T* () Tj T* (PRECIPITATION) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (Inside a cloud, the tiny drops bump into each other and join together, becoming) Tj T* (larger and heavier. When the drops grow too heavy for the air to hold up, they) Tj T* ET
endstream
